title: Salem2Start
---
<<declare $playerName>>

Entering the cafe this time had you salivating at the sight of
the desserts that were just baked. Salem was there, giggling as
two other girls darted around and chatted. As the wind chimes
announced your arrival, the two girls turned to you and greeted
you.

Salem: "Hi {$playerName}!"

She walked over to you, seeming happier today. She had skull
clips in her hair which complemented it.

Salem: "Come, me and my co workers made goodies!"

You were basically dragged to the counter, seeing racks of
different desserts. There were brownies, fifteens and caramel
squares.

Coworker: "Is this the person you've been talking about, Sal?"

They walked over to you.

Coworker: "They seem nice,"

Salem: "Yeah they're my friend,"

She said easily, walking to the counter to get a plastic plate.

You blinked at what she said. You wouldn’t consider yourself
friends, maybe acquaintances.

-> Set It Straight
    <<incRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump SetStraight>>

-> Question Her
    <<jump Question>>

-> Go with the Flow
    <<decRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump Flow>>
===

title: SetStraight
---
You: "Friends?"

You repeated, making Salem look over.

You: "Salem...we have only known each other for a few days,"

Salem suddenly looked flustered before the other two servers
giggled.

Coworker: "Ah Salem, ever the sweetheart,"

They rested their head on their hand while leaning over the
counter.

Coworker: "You must like {$playerName} a lot if you already
consider them a friend!"

The other teased, giggling as they leaned on Salem.

Salem whined in embarrassment, but let her coworker lean on her.
They seemed very close.

<<jump Dragged>>
===

title: Question
---
You: "You think we're friends?"

This made Salem splutter before her coworkers started giggling.

Coworker: "Ah Salem, ever the sweetheart,"

They leaned over the counter.

Coworker: "You must like {$playerName} a lot if you already
consider them a friend!"

Salem whined in embarrassment, letting her coworker lean on her.
They seemed very close.

<<jump Dragged>>
===

title: Flow
---
Despite not feeling the same about your relationship, you smiled
and nodded, not denying it.

Coworker: "You must like {$playerName} a lot if you already
consider them a friend!"

They teased, giggling as they leaned on Salem.

Salem whined in embarrassment, letting her coworker lean on her.
They seemed very close.

<<jump Dragged>>
===

title: Dragged
---
One of them dragged Salem off to cut the desserts. They chatted
away, giggling together, and soon you forgot what happened
yesterday.

Coworker: "I should thank you,"

You turned around and saw Salem's other coworker watching them.

Coworker: "You were there with Salem yesterday,"

You looked away and back to Salem, watching her laugh and squeak
as someone grabbed a brownie and ran away.

-> I had to do something
    <<incRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump HadTo>>

-> It wasn't that bad
    <<decRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump NotBad>>
===

title: HadTo
---
You couldn't have stayed still seeing how that server treated
Salem. It was wrong and made your blood boil.

You: "I had to do something,"

The server looked at you and nodded in agreement.

<<jump OneByOne>>
===

title: NotBad
---
You looked back to the day before, then to the server.

You: "I didn't think what happened yesterday was that bad,"

An awkward silence followed.

<<jump OneByOne>>
===

title: OneByOne
---
One by one, each batch of desserts was cut, and Salem picked up
a piece and walked over.

Salem: "Here {$playerName}, try some!"

She beamed, holding the snack up to your mouth.

You bit into it, and it tasted divine. She was a wonderful
baker.

You: "This is really good Salem,"

You said, taking another bite.

Salem didn't reply, so you looked at her. She gazed softly at
you with a gentle blush.

One of the girls nudged her, snapping her out of her daydream.
Stuttering, she pulled out a piece of paper from her apron.

<<jump LookingUp>>
===

title: LookingUp
---
Looking up, you were about to thank Salem before noticing how
nervous she looked. Her face tilted toward the window, eyes not
meeting yours.

Salem: "I feel like I may have answered a bit too seriously,"

She held her hands together.

Salem: "The question made me think a lot admittedly,"

You smiled and shook your head.

You: "Oh that's fine, it's what I need anyway,"

You slipped the note into your folder.

With that, Salem packed more desserts for you to take home. You
said goodbye before walking out.

<<pushObjectiveIndex "Doing the Rounds">>
===